Niles has no window function on its SQL surface (`over (partition by …)` is a parse error, NL0001/NL0009), and a posting's epoch — the task's order — is not a column a query can read (finding F8). The SQL-92 form, a self-join summing the earlier postings of the same account and currency, resolves its aliases since Niles fix 5/5, but it can only order by `txn`, which is a different query that coincides with this one only where epochs and txn ids happen to agree.
